# 📌 Project Overview

The Aespa Fanstore website consists of **6 webpages**:
1. Home (index.html)**
- Introduction to Aespa Fanstore  
- Featured image  
- Easy navigation  
- Footer with social links  

2. About (about.html)**
- Overview of the fanstore concept  
- FAQ section with **JavaScript accordion**  
- Clean layout and responsive typography  

3. Products (products.html)**
- Merchandise list  
- **Search filter (JS)**  
- **Lightbox image gallery** (JS)  

4. Events (events.html)**
- Full list of **Aespa SYNK : aeXIS LINE Tour (2025–2026)**  
- Aespa’s **confirmed 2025 MAMA Awards performance**  
- Clean card layout  

5. Enquiry (enquiry.html)**
- Enquiry form for product or event questions  
- **Client-side form validation**  
- **Success fade-in animation**  
- **AJAX-style simulated submission**  

6. Contact (contact.html)**
- General message contact form  
- **Full validation + error handling**  
- **AJAX fake submission**  
- Embedded Google Map  
- Local SEO section  

Responsive Design

The project is fully responsive using:
- CSS Flexbox  
- CSS Grid  
- Media queries  
- Mobile-first approach  
- Scalable typography  
- Responsive images  

Tested on:
- Desktop  
- Tablet  
- Mobile  
- Chrome Developer Tools  

JavaScript Features (Interactive Elements)

 Form Validation
- Checks input length  
- Email format validation  
- Required field checks  
- Red error messages for invalid fields  
- Success animation  

AJAX-Style Submission
- Prevents page reload  
- Simulates a server request  
- Displays a success message  

 Interactive Components
- FAQ accordion  
- Lightbox product gallery  
- Product search filter  
- Scroll-to-top button  
- DOM manipulation animations  

 Map Integration
- Google Maps iframe added to contact page  

---

 SEO Implementation

 On-Page SEO
- Meta descriptions  
- Meta keywords  
- Clean heading structure (H1, H2, H3)  
- Alt text on all images  
- Optimised filenames  
- Internal linking  
- Mobile-friendly layout  

 Off-Page SEO
- Footer links to Aespa’s official SNS  
- Local SEO (location section)  

 Additional Requirements
- `robots.txt`  
- `sitemap.xml`  
- Compressed images  
- Optimised page speed  
- Safe, validated inputs  

# 🔒 Security Measures

- Required fields enforced  
- JavaScript validation  
- Input length checks  
- Email format checks  
- Prevents blank or malformed submissions  

Testing Checklist

The site was tested across:
- Chrome  
- Safari  
- Edge  
- Mobile emulation  

Tests performed:
- All links working  

- Lightbox opens and closes

- FAQ accordion toggles correctly  

- Search filter filters live results  

- Scroll-to-top button appears on scroll 

- Forms show error messages  

- Forms show success messages 

- Responsive layout for all screen sizes  

Screenshots included in the repository.

# 📦 Deployment (GitHub Pages)

**How to run the site live:**

1. Upload repository to GitHub

2. Go to **Settings > Pages** 

3. Select branch: `main` 

4. Select folder: `/root`  

5. Save  

6. Wait 1–2 minutes for deployment  

